Dataset cf14071_repro_rlp_oneway {
  label: 'CF-14071 repro - forced rlp_propagation one_way'
  description: '''
    Same 8 models and same 8 edges as cf14071_repro (the customer's diagram). ONE difference: every
    relationship carries an EXPLICIT rlp_propagation='one_way'.

    WHY. Per Khai (2026-09-04), the docs are wrong on this point and he is updating them:

      - When rlp_propagation is OMITTED, it is 'two_way' by DEFAULT. It does NOT inherit filter_direction.
      - The reachability error is only raised when rlp_propagation is explicitly forced to 'one_way'.

    That resolves why cf14071_repro does not error. It has filter_direction 'one_way' everywhere but no
    rlp_propagation, so RLP propagation was two_way the whole time, every model was reachable, and there was
    correctly nothing to complain about.

    So THIS dataset is the one that should reproduce the customer's error. Forcing one_way pins RLP to
    dimension -> fact, so it leaves Dim Store, reaches Fact Sales and Fact SOH, and cannot climb into Dim
    Date to cross to the benchmark side. Expect the three pink boxes from the diagram to be unreachable:

      - Fact Sales (Benchmark)
      - Fact SOH (Benchmark)
      - Dim Region (Benchmark)

      "Some permission rules are not applied in this Explore. This is likely due to a missing relationship
       between the models."

    Per the doc's own logic it should also break the CORE side, since Dim Date and Dim Region also sit
    behind one-way edges from the facts. Worth checking both:

      1. Sales $ alone                     -> expect 300 (vendor_id = 1, store 1's only row).
      2. Sales $ by Dim Date -> Date       -> error? This is the core-side equivalent of the doc's
                                              "total_orders by dim_products.name" query.
      3. Benchmark Sales $ alone           -> error, or 20500?
      4. Sales $ + Benchmark Sales $        -> error?

    OBSERVED IN cf14071_repro (rlp_propagation omitted, i.e. two_way), as an Explorer with vendor_id = 1:
      Sales $ = restricted correctly, dim_store lookup showed only store 1
      Benchmark Sales $ = 20500, UNFILTERED, no error
      both metrics together = no error

    Note that last result is itself worth raising: if RLP propagation really is two_way by default, the
    store filter should have travelled Dim Store -> Fact Sales -> UP into Dim Date -> DOWN into Fact Sales
    (Benchmark) and narrowed the benchmark to store 1's only date (20260102), giving 13000 (7000 + 6000),
    not 20500. It did not. So either RLP does not traverse through an intermediate FACT table, or two_way
    propagation governs reachability without actually applying the filter across that path.

    Either way, the practical finding for CF-14071 is that the customer's requirement already works today:
    filter_direction 'one_way' with rlp_propagation left at its default gives store-restricted core facts,
    a fully unrestricted benchmark cohort, and both metrics in one report with no error.
  '''
  data_source_name: 'demodb'

  models: [
    dim_store,
    dim_region,
    dim_date,
    dim_region_benchmark,
    fact_sales,
    fact_soh,
    fact_sales_benchmark,
    fact_soh_benchmark,
  ]

  relationships: [
    // Dim Store -> core facts. RLP forced one_way: dim -> fact only, no climbing back out.
    relationship(fact_sales.store_key > dim_store.store_key, true, 'one_way', rlp_propagation='one_way'),
    relationship(fact_soh.store_key > dim_store.store_key, true, 'one_way', rlp_propagation='one_way'),

    // Dim Region -> core facts.
    relationship(fact_sales.region_key > dim_region.region_key, true, 'one_way', rlp_propagation='one_way'),
    relationship(fact_soh.region_key > dim_region.region_key, true, 'one_way', rlp_propagation='one_way'),

    // Dim Date -> Fact Sales and Fact Sales (Benchmark). This is the edge whose blocked upward hop is
    // supposed to strand the benchmark side.
    relationship(fact_sales.date_key > dim_date.date_key, true, 'one_way', rlp_propagation='one_way'),
    relationship(fact_sales_benchmark.date_key > dim_date.date_key, true, 'one_way', rlp_propagation='one_way'),

    // Dim Region (Benchmark) -> benchmark facts.
    relationship(fact_sales_benchmark.region_key > dim_region_benchmark.region_key, true, 'one_way', rlp_propagation='one_way'),
    relationship(fact_soh_benchmark.region_key > dim_region_benchmark.region_key, true, 'one_way', rlp_propagation='one_way'),
  ]

  permission store_reporting_proprietor_permissions {
    field: r(dim_store.store_key)
    operator: 'matches_user_attribute'
    value: 'vendor_id'
  }
}
